=E2=80=98Like a movie script=E2=80=99: Michael McArdle backs Northern Irela=
nd to make history


Manager says he has made team =E2=80=98playoff ready=E2=80=99 since taking =
over in March. They now face Portugal in their quest to reach World Cup


Northern Ireland's Keri Halliday (centre) is greeted by manager Michael McA=
rdle during a World Cup 2027 qualifier. Photograph: Liam McBurney/PA


Tom Garry


For seven and a half years, Michael McArdle worked in the construction indu=
stry while playing semi-professional football, studying for a degree in bui=
lding services engineering and raising three young children together with h=
is wife. Any leftover earnings he put into funding his football coaching ba=
dges.

Eventually he took a big risk and decided to take =E2=80=9Cprobably a 300% =
drop in salary=E2=80=9D and commit to coaching, a life-changing moment that=
 now may be leading towards a World Cup in Brazil next summer as the
